{"kind":"event","event_id":2913,"event_uid":"01M2J6483FCJJ2BGXJV21KKRQ4","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":152,"issue_uid":"01M2J62J2DDS32RC7CW5KCGK5S","issue_short_id":"gk5s","actor":"impl:1@run-137","hlc_physical_ms":1789464289391,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"99e076839261fe489c8d602070346dc75830b40651b45cffbe4b4f83d2dc416a","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J6483E99MM1HV15HWKXS6M","author":"impl:1@run-137","body":"Task 1 start. Approach: add evaluate_stale_if(tasks, base_tree) -> (refusals, advisories) to skills/ultrapowers/scripts/compile_plan.py, reading BASE through the existing BaseTree seam (git ls-tree for a sha base, disk + git hash-object for a directory base), gh issue view for issue predicates with a process-wide per-number cache. Refusals join collect_violations' list before the verdict; advisories print after, beside the BASE fact: lines. Then two sentences into skills/ultrawrite/SKILL.md §The proof gate. No test of my own — the exam at tests/test_compile_plan_edges.py is a peer's.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:24:49.390351461Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:24:49.391Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2928,"event_uid":"01M2J65544WA6XGWB6MK9ED0GG","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":153,"issue_uid":"01M2J62NE7DCQ9BZAR12625G1Q","issue_short_id":"5g1q","actor":"impl:2@run-137","hlc_physical_ms":1789464319108,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"b53368caabdc0cad650d5bbf1d7ce7236a342b8e592320fbb030f390e9774bc7","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J65543DHQSAABDGZQGBWG3","author":"impl:2@run-137","body":"Task 2 approach: three edits, no new behavior beyond the filter. (1) fleet/launch.mjs:625 — the clean-compile return keeps lines starting `STALE fact:` beside `BASE fact:`, in stdout order; the doc comment above it gains the same sentence. M2 (the exit-2 refusal carrying the compiler's `STALE fact:` line) and M3 (renderLaunch spreading baseFacts last) already hold at BASE and are pinned, not changed. (2) fleet/RUNBOOK.md §Per run line 219 and (3) CLAUDE.md's fleet/ Layout bullet each gain `STALE fact:` beside `BASE fact:`. fleet/tests/test_launch_compile_facts.mjs is the peer's exam path — I write no test file there; I check the legs from a scratch script under /tmp and delete it.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:19.107471464Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:19.108Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2930,"event_uid":"01M2J65YGDFDD4E03CPCCECVDW","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":152,"issue_uid":"01M2J62J2DDS32RC7CW5KCGK5S","issue_short_id":"gk5s","actor":"exam:1@run-137","hlc_physical_ms":1789464345101,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"9c643ad5fd6f6619fdcb056f52565ec5282241654c2ea1164ead7f9630b52083","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J65YGCSFXFENGDNVQAB9DY","author":"exam:1@run-137","body":"Examiner: writing the exam for task 1 into tests/test_compile_plan_edges.py, appended below the existing eleven proof-run/Check: cases (which stay untouched — they are bare --check/plain compiles and the template's Stale-if entries never hold in the temp repo).\n\nApproach, leg by leg:\n- One module-scope fixture builds a real git repo under tmp_path: git init + commit present.py, plus a bin/ dir for the fake gh. Plans are written INSIDE that repo with the file's own _write_plan, so a 40-hex --base resolves in the plan's own toplevel.\n- Every path/sha/issue row runs twice where the leg says so: --base <dir> and --base <HEAD sha>.\n- The Stale-if entries of the shared TASK_1/TASK_2 templates are substituted textually (task 2 keeps path-exists: `fleet/reader.mjs`, which does not hold in the temp repo), so make_plan/_write_plan are reused unchanged.\n- Refusals assert the exact line 'STALE fact: task <id>: <entry> holds at BASE' by equality against a stdout line, with <entry> carrying its backticks verbatim as parse_task leaves it; PLAN OK rows assert the first stdout line is exactly PLAN OK and exit 0.\n- The fake gh is a shell script reading its answer from a file beside it and appending its argv to a log; the 'no gh' row builds a PATH of one dir holding only a symlink to the real git, since the compiler is invoked by absolute interpreter path.\n- (f) asserts exit 0, first stdout line PLAN OK, and a line beginning 'STALE fact: task 1: <entry> unreadable at BASE — ' (prefix only; the reason wording is unpinned).\n- (h) runs the Proof's Run: line verbatim through bash at ROOT.\n\nChecked at BASE first: STALE_PREDICATE_RE only requires the head + colon, so the malformed rows of (f) still parse; the only base-gated refusal in collect_violations today is the Delete:-absent-at-BASE one, and these plans have no Delete:, so a --base compile of them is PLAN OK at BASE — which is exactly why each holds-row is red for the one right reason.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:45.100108655Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:45.101Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2932,"event_uid":"01M2J66YMYAS4D5C2KZXYNKRT3","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":153,"issue_uid":"01M2J62NE7DCQ9BZAR12625G1Q","issue_short_id":"5g1q","actor":"exam:2@run-137","hlc_physical_ms":1789464378014,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"ef19b4d831f1d2b5973a08b010ca62ba1f996de00cd310a82c4084e8215805e8","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J66YMXQFS9106KQR7FDHCD","author":"exam:2@run-137","body":"exam-2 (examiner): writing fleet/tests/test_launch_compile_facts.mjs as a hermetic, spawn-free sim. Plan, leg by leg: (a) [M1] a recording fake exec answering exit 0 with PLAN OK / one BASE fact: / the M1 STALE fact: advisory / one note: line — verifyPlanCompiles resolves to exactly those two fact lines, deep-equal, in stdout order (a STALE-before-BASE stdout pins 'stdout order' rather than a fixed BASE-first sort), and PLAN OK alone resolves to []. (b) [M2] exit 2 with the backticked 'STALE fact: task 1: path-exists: `present.py` holds at BASE' on stdout rejects with a Refusal (instanceof, from ../lobby.mjs) whose message carries 'compile_plan.py --check --base', 'refused' and that line verbatim; the fake is asserted called exactly once, cmd 'python3', argv carrying --check and --base <base>. (c) [M3] renderLaunch over a plain object — no launch driven — whose baseFacts is ['BASE fact: x','STALE fact: y']: the last two lines of the joined text equal those two in that order; the same object without baseFacts renders text containing neither. (d) [M4] the two Run: greps re-expressed as in-process reads: the RUNBOOK '## Per run' section (line-range read, next '## ' heading ends it) joined on spaces matches /BASE fact:.*STALE fact:.*launch line/, and CLAUDE.md names 'STALE fact:' with its '## Layout'..'## Doctrine' range matching /compile_plan.py --check --base.*STALE fact:/. No network, no spawn, no absolute literal outside the checkout; imports are ../launch.mjs and ../lobby.mjs only, and it ends on ALL TESTS PASSED. Expected red at BASE: (a) resolves to the BASE fact line alone (line 625 filters only 'BASE fact:') and (d) finds no STALE fact: in either doc; (b) and (c) are green at BASE by design — the task pins the refusal path and renderLaunch as unchanged surfaces.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:26:18.013563527Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:26:18.014Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2934,"event_uid":"01M2J68D3H5FXPS517QS3XYTMV","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":153,"issue_uid":"01M2J62NE7DCQ9BZAR12625G1Q","issue_short_id":"5g1q","actor":"impl:2@run-137","hlc_physical_ms":1789464425585,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"449c8ea5d6ab6f42846e30a021beb50fc92fbfce8cb8eecfca51ecfe48b91a94","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J68D3GAZM20EZX5HMG23WQ","author":"impl:2@run-137","body":"Done at 4ff5e792 (base a94143bb). Footprint: fleet/launch.mjs, fleet/RUNBOOK.md, CLAUDE.md — no test file written (fleet/tests/test_launch_compile_facts.mjs is the peer's exam path). fleet/launch.mjs:625 now keeps `STALE fact:` lines beside `BASE fact:` ones, in stdout order; the doc comment above verifyPlanCompiles says the same and notes that a `STALE fact:` on a clean compile is the advisory kind while a predicate that holds is the exit-2 refusal. M2 and M3 needed no code: the refusal message already carries the compiler's text verbatim through output(res), and renderLaunch already spreads result.baseFacts last — I checked both from a scratch node script on stdin (no file), together with M1 and the empty case. Both `Run:` legs pass; the Check leg is clean. test_launch_bump, test_launch_size, test_launch_kata_seed, test_doctor_rows, test_janitor, test_sandbox_boot_viz and test_sims_are_hermetic (25 sims swept, 0 offenders) all still print ALL TESTS PASSED.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:27:05.584433367Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:27:05.585Z"}
